course: dictionary
lesson: 4892
title: Ignore and what it really means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ignore is a verb, and it means to pay no attention to someone or something on purpose. It also means not doing anything about something you should notice, like a warning. The word on purpose is the key clue, because ignoring is a choice.
explain: Look at the words around it to be sure which meaning fits. «Ignoring friends' greetings» tells you someone is being left out, because the greeting is not answered. Check by swapping in a meaning: "not paying attention on purpose" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Ignore changes its form to fit the time. «She ignored the rude comment» is about the past, «He is ignoring the warning» is happening now, and «Don't ignore bullying» is a command. Ignores, ignored and ignoring all come from the same word.
fact: Ignore means to pay no attention to someone or something on purpose.
fact: To ignore a warning means not acting on it, even though you should notice it.
fact: «Ignoring friends' greetings» often makes them feel hurt and less likely to include you.
fact: Some things should never be ignored: a warning sign, an alarm, or pain.
fact: «Don't ignore bullying»: tell an adult. Online, ignore and block messages from strangers.
exercise: «Ignoring friends' greetings often makes them feel hurt.» What does ignoring mean here? | Giving a present | Saying hello loudly | *Not paying attention on purpose | Waving back
exercise: A sign says «Danger: deep water». What should you not do? | *Ignore the warning | Stay back | Tell an adult | Read the sign
exercise: If a number you do not know calls you, what is the safest choice? | *Let a parent answer or ignore it | Answer and give your address | Call it back straight away | Post the number online
test: Which word means to pay no attention to someone on purpose? | Warn | *Ignore | Notice | Greet
test: Mum says, «Never ignore pain.» What should you do if you feel pain? | Ignore it for a while | Pretend it is not there | *Tell an adult | Keep it quiet and hope it goes
exam: Which is the safest thing to do when you see a warning sign? | Take a photo of it and laugh | Ignore it and walk on | Push past it | *Take it seriously and stop
